# Auto-detect text files and normalize line endings to LF inside the
# repository itself. This is a baseline only - the entries below force LF
# on checkout too (regardless of platform or a contributor's local
# core.autocrlf setting) for files that must have real Unix line endings
# to function at all.
* text=auto

# --- Files that execute directly on the Ubuntu VPS via a shebang, or are
#     parsed by Nginx/consumed as shell config. A CRLF-terminated shebang
#     line ("#!/usr/bin/env bash\r") fails to exec on Linux, and a
#     trailing \r can corrupt Nginx directive values. These must always
#     check out with LF, even on a Windows contributor's machine. ---
*.sh            text eol=lf
m3u8-manager    text eol=lf
install.sh      text eol=lf
uninstall.sh    text eol=lf
status.sh       text eol=lf
*.template      text eol=lf
*.conf          text eol=lf

# --- Explicit binary types ---
# None currently exist in this project (no images, fonts, or archives are
# checked in), but these are declared defensively so Git never attempts a
# text/EOL conversion on them if one is added later. HLS .ts segments are
# NOT listed here - they are already excluded from the repository entirely
# by path-scoped rules in .gitignore (hls/, web/hls/, etc.), so a global
# binary rule would only cost future TypeScript .ts source files their
# normal Git diffs for no actual benefit.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.eot   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
*.tar   binary
*.mp4   binary
